    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "There is a diversity issue within the music industry: only 2% of music producers are womxn .\r\nThe principal goal of ProduceHER is to increase the number of working womxn producers within the music industry by providing a safe environment for womxn producers to practice and hone their skills, receive constructive feedback from reputable sources, and build networking skills, all while improving self-efficacy and encouraging sense of belonging within the field.\r\nWhile there are several existing solutions that assist in introducing womxn to music production careers, there are still many barriers in the music industry for these womxn producers to get hired and recognized, and to be considered skillful in the field. There exists no wide scale environment that mitigates this recognition barrier successfully, and this often leaves aspiring womxn producers discouraged and unmotivated towards pursuing the music industry professionally.\r\nIn order for an aspiring womxn music producer to go from a place of limited opportunities and exposure (losing interest/motivation in the field) to developing a continued, motivated, and lucrative interest in production, she must have a welcoming environment and opportunities to practice and expand her skills, feel welcome and able to use her skills and talents, and have availability to role models, mentorships, and recruiters .\r\nProduceHER focuses on giving womxn producers a safe environment to show and develop their skills through receiving feedback from established producers, production shops, and recruiters while mitigating the recognition barrier; this feedback environment will help increase focused visibility amongst recruiters, increase womxn producer self-efficacy, and combat the problem of stereotype threat and discounting womxn producers’ skills.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
